{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"Main_Section": "**7. ARTICLE 5(1)(F) AI ACT EMOTION RECOGNITION**", "Sub_Section": "**7.1.Rationale and objectives**", "Letter_Section": "**_d) On the basis of their biometric data_**", "source": "clean_eu_proh_ai_act.md"}, "page_content": "- An AI system inferring emotions from key stroke (way of typing), facial expressions, body postures or movements is based on biometric data and falls within the scope of the prohibition.  \n- (252) The AI Act definition of biometric data is therefore broad and includes any biometric data used for emotion recognition, biometric categorisation or other purposes.<sup>160</sup>", "type": "Document"}}